ies to the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"next","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" session started in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"process, never to one already running. There is no warning for a late call, because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the process cannot tell a mistimed call apart from correct setup for the next session.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Unlike ","type":"text"},{"code":"declareProduct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which ignores a conflicting second call, this is last write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wins. The SDK appends the platform suffix, so pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"appium","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"appium-ios","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"productComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that sanitizes to nothing leaves the previous value in place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than clearing it; the ","type":"text"},{"code":"actor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the same call still applies.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axedevtoolsxcui\/axeintegration\/setusage(actor:productcomponent:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]},{"paths":["\/documentation\/axedevtoolsxcui\/axeintegration\/setusage(actor:productcomponent:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Called once per process by the integrating layer (the Appium driver, the Desktop","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Analyzer, MCP) to say who triggered this session and which product surface it came"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"from. Public so those layers can call it; deliberately absent from customer docs and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"not part of the supported surface.","typ